<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander von Humboldt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1769">1769</a>–<a href="/years/1859">1859</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander von Humboldt was a Prussian naturalist, geographer and explorer. From 1799 to 1804 he travelled through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-america">Spanish America</a> with the botanist Aimé Bonpland, and his Political Essay on the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> described <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>'s population, mines and economy. His work helped found modern physical geography, and his multi-volume Kosmos sought to describe the unity of nature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-von-humboldt.jpg" alt="Alexander von Humboldt" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Karl Stieler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stieler,_Joseph_Karl_-_Alexander_von_Humboldt_-_1843.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
